    "reasoning": "The task requires a venue for ~90 guests, catering allowed, and short-notice Saturday availability. Lakeview: PUBLIC.1 confirms outdoor seating for up to 120 (capacity sufficient); S01 (my own source) reports its only access road is closed by flooding and expected impassable through the weekend, which covers Saturday night, so access is a serious concern. However, S01 speaks only to that access road and does not establish that the resort itself is closed, unavailable, or without any alternative arrangement; the local reconstruction correctly notes the geographic scope (the single access road) and time limit (through the weekend). Grand Oak: PUBLIC.2 says it usually requires two weeks' notice, directly conflicting with short notice, and its capacity is only qualitative ('largest ballroom'). Heritage: PUBLIC.3 says catering restrictions may apply to non-packaged food, leaving catering unresolved; A3's private no-catering claim is not my own inspected evidence. No venue is fully confirmed on all criteria, so any choice is tentative. Lakeview is the best supported: it has confirmed numeric capacity, no categorical restriction stated in the public evidence, and the only defect is a single-source access report that does not itself prove the venue is unusable. Grand Oak's notice requirement is a categorical scheduling conflict, and Heritage's catering uncertainty strikes at a core requirement. I therefore retain the historical tentative choice of Lakeview, narrowed to a conditional pick pending confirmation of road access, this-Saturday availability, and catering permission.",
